   b) IMMUTABLE SIGNATURE LOGIC: The core signature injected into the 
      system's 'build.prop' (specifically targeting 'ro.build.display.id' 
      or equivalent lines via 'sed' or patching scripts) MUST NOT be deleted, 
      overwritten, or fully replaced. 
      
      If a derived fork modifies this tool, the final generated property 
      value MUST preserve the original authorship. It is strictly forbidden 
      to wipe the original credit. The signature string must maintain a 
      co-existence format, explicitly showing that it is a derivative work.
      (e.g., "Built by [YourForkName], a fork of CSM by Minhmc2077").

